# Giant Beaver: "target creature that saddled it this turn" must still be a creature on the battlefield (CR 115.1, 702.171c). Turn 3: three Memnites saddle the Beaver (power 3), then a
# Lightning Bolt (Mox Ruby) kills Memnite #3 before attackers: it saddled the Beaver this turn but is gone, so it is refused as the target; Memnite #1 is chosen and grows to a 2/2.

[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Giant Beaver
Mox Emerald
Mox Ruby
Memnite
Memnite
Memnite
Lightning Bolt
Plains x12

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Green)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Giant Beaver.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Memnite.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Memnite.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Memnite.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Giant Beaver.Activate
Bot1.Choose(Memnite#1; Memnite#2; Memnite#3)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Lightning Bolt.Cast(Bot1.Battlefield.Memnite#3)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot1.Battlefield.Giant Beaver.Saddled = true
[T3 Bot1.DeclareAttackers]
Bot1.Attack(Giant Beaver > Bot2)
! Bot1.Target(Bot1.Graveyard.Memnite)
Bot1.Target(Bot1.Battlefield.Memnite#1)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot1.Battlefield.Memnite#1.Power = 2

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield.Memnite#1.Toughness = 2
Bot1.Graveyard.Count = 3
